From 521df9ece3346207713b666eb23bc8df57fbc111 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fil Dunsky <filipp.dunsky@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 11:25:10 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: cortina: add checked native Wi-Fi flowtable forwarding

Delegate supported ath9k and ath10k flows to the forwarding engine while
retaining normal MAC encryption, packet numbers and TX status. Validate
immutable receive identities before delivery or ordinary software fallback.
Retire result graphs and endpoint labels only after reference withdrawal
and bounded fixed-profile quiescence; quarantine uncertain ownership.

Initialize translated skb IP headers before normal Wi-Fi TX. Document
physical correctness checks, the measured throughput correction and
the remaining workload and hardware-qualification limits.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Fil Dunsky <filipp.dunsky@gmail.com>

--- a/Documentation/networking/device_drivers/ethernet/cortina/cs7542-flowtable.rst
+++ b/Documentation/networking/device_drivers/ethernet/cortina/cs7542-flowtable.rst
@@ -22,7 +22,8 @@ publishing a lookup. Unsupported request
 IPv6 uses exact 128-bit addresses without NAT66/NPTv6. Extension headers,
 fragments, link-local/multicast destinations and non-TCP/UDP traffic stay
 in software. IPv6 route and NDP changes revoke affected admission, as do
-ICMPv6 Packet Too Big messages. Wi-Fi acceleration is not enabled.
+ICMPv6 Packet Too Big messages. The native Wi-Fi paths described below
+extend the physical wired-port frontend without changing NAT66 policy.
 
 TCP admission additionally requires an established conntrack state. The
 flowtable supplies that state together with the route MTU. SYN, FIN,
@@ -44,21 +45,69 @@ FDB, neighbours, route MTU and the same
 An observed ambiguity, withdrawn flow or pending invalidation cannot use
 this path. It does not admit a new unobserved flow or fabricate activity.
 
+Native Wi-Fi path
+-----------------
+
+An optional mac80211 net_setup_tc callback attests an AR9580 or QCA9880 PCI
+STA/AP interface to the built-in owner. Both endpoints must remain in the
+initial network namespace. Missing support, unsupported interfaces and
+ambiguous route, neighbour or bridge-FDB observations retain software
+forwarding.
+
+The owner copies admitted wireless input into the ordinary network-engine
+TX queue and consumes the original only after successful publication. A
+CPU3 miss returns the unedited packet through CPU1. An edited CPU1 result
+requires a live immutable receipt matching CLASS, HIT forwarding result,
+format epoch, interface label, tuple and Ethernet identity before normal
+native Wi-Fi transmission. Unknown edited results are dropped rather than
+sent through software NAT again. Checked input and output fences stop new
+admission and drain old readers before interface references are released.
+
+This is forwarding-engine NAT/routing through the native MAC stack, not PE
+firmware or Wi-Fi DMA takeover. Encryption, packet numbers and TX status
+remain with native ath9k/ath10k and mac80211. It requires no laboratory
+mailbox, PE session or additional reserved-memory region. The unchanged
+network engine still requires its normal top-of-DDR QM reservation. A
+missing native callback keeps the interface on the software path.
+
 Resource lifetime
 -----------------
 
-There are 16 admitted direction selectors and eight immutable result
-records in this implementation. A result includes every hardware-visible
-forwarding dependency. Identical results may be shared by independent
-selectors. A retired selector may be rebound only after invalidation and
-complete readback, with the original immutable result still present.
-Removing one selector does not retire another selector sharing its result.
-
-This is not general result reclamation. An incompatible result consumes
-another record. Eight different retained results exhaust this small
-allocation pool until a verified complete network-engine reset. Further
-flows fall back to software. A successful lookup withdrawal is not treated
-as proof that all in-flight hardware references have drained.
+The implementation admits up to 16 simultaneous direction selectors and
+eight result graphs. A live result includes every hardware-visible
+forwarding dependency and remains immutable while referenced. Identical
+results may be shared. Removing one selector does not retire its neighbour.
+
+The built-in owner can reclaim a native graph only when every member is
+withdrawn and no backend cookie refers to it. It verifies inactive CLASS
+images, all historical hash affinities, overflow and retained ACL state.
+Lookup withdrawal alone does not establish retirement of in-flight work.
+
+For the fixed external-DDR profile, the owner pauses common NI receive
+calendar admission and allows IRQ/NAPI buffer returns to run. It requires
+empty NI state, matching packet-engine counters and all expected QM/TM
+buffer credits, observed unchanged for at least 100 microseconds. An
+independent hard timer restores admission at a two-millisecond deadline.
+Expiry or busy state refuses reclamation. These are measured conditions
+on this profile, not a documented universal silicon retirement command.
+
+Only after that observation does the owner clear parent and dependent
+table rows with readback. It then releases graph slots and historical
+bucket affinities. Class-scoped ACL traps remain immutable; rebinding
+checks their retained image. Generations, version fences and selector
+high-water history are preserved. Uncertain transactions retain ownership
+and quarantine admission. No FE/QM/TM reset or HIT bitmap clear is used.
+The simultaneous pool limits remain unchanged; unsupported or currently
+full/busy cases use software.
+
+Wireless endpoint labels use a separate, non-wrapping software generation.
+An unregistered interface alone does not release its hardware label:
+retained leases and receive identities continue to pin that label. Once
+those references are gone, the owner drains old RCU readers, verifies
+completion of the Linux TX DMA ring and requires the same engine quiet
+condition before reusing the label. A busy drain can use a never-published
+label instead; exhaustion falls back to software.
+This does not require an engine reset or reuse a previous software epoch.
 
 Failed or ambiguous hardware transactions close admission and retain the
 state needed for isolation and recovery. The current replaceable modules
@@ -85,6 +134,109 @@ not evidence of uninterrupted hardware r
 Validation and provenance
 -------------------------
 
+Additional installed-image checks on 28 November exercised plain routed
+IPv6 through ath9k STA and AP on both radios. The ath10k AP software and
+hardware TCP/UDP controls each returned 100 exact replies. Both hardware
+directions showed fresh chip HIT transitions and no marked LAN1 frames
+after warmup. Ath9k STA TCP returned 400 exact replies with two fresh
+HIT transitions; thirteen postwarm frames used the CPU over forty seconds.
+Ath9k AP TCP returned 400 exact replies. Its UDP run returned 97/100
+compared with 99/100 in the software control; these are not zero-loss
+or endurance qualifications. TCP and UDP retain ordinary software fallback.
+
+Matched software/hardware UDP traces placed the newly observed missing
+requests beyond the Wi-Fi stack TX boundary, absent from the host echo
+server, with no capture overflow. A host scan reproduced common delays.
+This does not retrospectively prove the cause of an older DNS timeout.
+The initial pipelined TCP echo comparison measured software flowtable
+111/119 and hardware 51/57 Mbit/s on this WLAN/host path. A later review
+found missing skb network/transport offsets on translated Wi-Fi output.
+Fresh RX skbs bypassed the receive stack and reached the MAC classifier
+with an unset IP header. Initialize those offsets after receipt/packet
+validation and internal label removal, before handing the frame to Linux.
+Two reversed-order framed echo pairs in a normal-root RAM boot measured
+hardware 105.5/111.1 and software 112.4/99.6 Mbit/s, with exact data and
+fresh chip HIT transitions in both directions. The matching full image
+then passed read-only RAM/automatic return before NAND installation.
+Installed kernel and five module payloads were checked against the image.
+
+Standard iperf3 on that installed image measured hardware/software
+168.7/143.8 Mbit/s from LAN to WAN and 269.5/249.7 in reverse. Each test
+used one TCP stream, two seconds of omitted warmup and eight measured
+seconds. Simultaneous hardware/software controls shared the same radio
+window: 90.9/92.4 Mbit/s outward and 155.6/113.5 in reverse. Traffic was
+local: a LAN namespace, Almond+ 5GHz STA, the existing AP and PC Wi-Fi.
+An earlier post-install echo window stalled both modes, with long TCP
+draining; its cause is not established and those results are retained.
+These short checks do not establish endurance, an ASIC line rate or a
+performance advantage across other radios, roles or traffic patterns.
+
+The later label-lifetime kernel image received compatible native MAC
+module APK updates. A contended BIND returns unsupported to nft so that
+NETDEV_REGISTER can retain its software hook while holding RTNL. Later
+ordinary flowtable binding admits hardware forwarding. UNBIND errors
+remain unchanged.
+
+The installed combination exercised eight real AP interface removal/
+creation cycles. The opaque owner API observed reused
+hardware VIDs with strictly increasing software epochs. The independent
+watchdog bounded teardown, and an ordinary reboot returned to OpenWrt
+with the original settings and UI. Model checks separately covered
+20,000 allocator reuses, retained leases/receipts and failure quarantine.
+
+
+An installed 28 November personal image with backend 10 checked distinct
+UDP SNAT actions from physical LAN1 through native ath10k STA WAN to an
+external DNS endpoint. Thirty different translated-port actions completed
+360 nonce-checked replies with no marked CPU LAN1 frames after warmup.
+First-packet controls verified the capture path. The same NAND boot
+performed 59 graph reclaims without resetting the engine;
+a live neighbouring socket completed 321 replies without error.
+Ordinary conservative flowtable expiry may renew its internal selectors;
+the test retains that distinction instead of requiring permanent IDs.
+
+These are bounded correctness checks, not throughput or endurance tests.
+The total combines qualified phases from three partial fixture runs and
+a final nine-flow pass. Earlier fixture stops covered overly strict
+selector/readiness assumptions and one UDP timeout whose cause was not
+established; its neighbouring flow continued. That event is retained,
+and these measurements are not a zero-loss qualification. The final
+paced segment needed no UDP retransmission.
+
+Earlier installed backend-9 checks additionally qualify AP IPv4 NAT on
+both radios and plain routed IPv6 through ath10k STA WAN. The new graph
+churn test does not rerun or relabel those earlier protocol/role matrices.
+Native Wi-Fi encryption and TX status remain with the normal MAC drivers.
+The personal image's unused laboratory reservation is absent from the
+public target DT; complete configurations are not identical.
+
+
+On 27 November the native ath9k path was checked on installed Almond+
+OpenWrt 6.18.64, from physical LAN1 to an AR9580 2.4 GHz STA Wi-Fi WAN.
+For TCP and UDP, twelve nonce-checked DNS replies completed with the normal
+firewall4 hardware-offload flag, HW_OFFLOAD, fresh owned ASIC HIT transitions
+in both directions and zero marked CPU LAN1 frames. The TCP software
+control contained 24 marked frames. Original UCI settings were restored;
+both tests used the same normal NAND boot without another kernel launch.
+
+A subsequent installed normal image also qualifies the QCA9880 native
+ath10k STA WAN at 5180 MHz. TCP and UDP each completed twelve exact DNS
+replies with the ordinary hardware flag, fresh owned ASIC HIT transitions
+in both directions and zero marked CPU LAN1 frames. Both software controls
+recorded twelve replies and 24 frames. The 5 GHz packet checks share one
+normal NAND boot; temporary configuration and PC routing were restored.
+Read-only samples during warmup retain a fresh HIT transition even if a
+later identical rearm refreshes the current sticky-bit baseline.
+
+Those checks qualify IPv4 NAT for the two STA WAN paths. Later AP LAN
+and Wi-Fi IPv6 checks are recorded above, under a separate installed
+source/configuration scope. They are not a throughput,
+endurance or full 802.11 processing-acceleration claim. The personal
+test image retained an unused laboratory memory reservation;
+that reservation and its boot marker are excluded from the public draft.
+Kernel/DT boot qualification and packet evidence must retain that distinction.
+
+
 IPv6 is a local development extension to the published IPv4 RFC. On
 Almond+ it was checked in a RAM kernel with physical LAN1 and WAN ports
 and the ordinary firewall4 hardware-offload setting. For each of TCP and
@@ -126,7 +278,8 @@ Review questions
